<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Oct 24 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>Belgium     167,000-A			 Nil</p>
<p>Japan	 108,700</p>
<p>Netherlands 101,900 Mexico	 95,700</p>
<p>France	 50,400</p>
<p>China	  50,000</p>
<p>A-includes news sales of 92,000 and 75,000 in destination changes.</p>
<p>Net sales of 810,100 tonnes were 42 percent below last week's marketing year high, 18 percent under the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 699,300 tonnes -- a marketing year high -- were 17 percent above the previous week and double the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Taiwan (170,400), Japan (116,500), Mexico (85,100), Belgium (79,000) and South Korea (74,900).</p>
</text>
